{# Transcribed from the static design mockup (verify page). STEP PROGRESS moved into
   partials/stepper.twig (Verify & Review active, no progress fill — the three earlier
   connectors render as completed/checkmark).

   `[22.13]`–`[22.21]`: the mockup's controls are a real form here. The page
   posts to /verify/ and works with scripting off; theme/js/verify.js only guards
   against a doubled click.

   DEVIATION from the design source — the ID upload. The mockup's dropzone and camera
   button are kept as markup because the design is a deliverable, and rendered DISABLED
   because nothing here receives a document: `[22.21]` puts identity documents under a
   retention policy that is not built, and a control that accepts a file and discards it
   is worse than one that says so. The form is not multipart, so no file can be sent
   even if the attribute were removed by hand. The mockup's two paragraphs promising an
   upload are replaced for the same reason — they described something the storefront
   cannot do.

   DEVIATION from the design source — the SSN box. Rendered only when identity checks
   are live AND a configured check actually names `ssn` (see
   VerificationStep::collectsSsn()). In the shipped configuration it is absent: asking
   for the most sensitive datum in the funnel for a check that cannot run is what
   `[22.21]` forbids. #}
{% extends 'layouts/funnel.twig' %}
{% set page_title = 'Intake: Verify & Review' %}
{% set page_description = 'AsterMD intake: securely verify your identity to complete your physician review.' %}
{% block content %}

  <!-- ==================== STEP PROGRESS ==================== -->
  {% include 'partials/stepper.twig' with {
    steps: [
      { label: 'Eligibility', icon: 'gauge' },
      { label: 'Contact', icon: 'user' },
      { label: 'Medical', icon: 'list-ordered' },
      { label: 'Verify & Review', icon: 'user-check' },
    ],
    active: 4,
  } %}

  <!-- ==================== SECURE IDENTITY VERIFICATION ==================== -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-[660px] px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="font-heading text-center text-[24px] font-bold leading-tight sm:text-[28px] text-heading">Secure Identity Verification</h1>

    {% if verification_notice is defined and verification_notice %}
      {# `[20.1]`: only a refused identity is styled and worded as a failed check. An
         inconclusive outcome — the provider deciding nothing, our own request being
         rejected, the integration being inactive — is not a statement about the buyer.

         verification_held is a separate flag and carries no colour of its own: it says the
         journey has stopped here, which is worth announcing to a screen reader whatever the
         outcome behind it, and is not a claim that anything is wrong with the buyer. #}
      <p role="{{ verification_failed|default(false) or verification_held|default(false) ? 'alert' : 'status' }}" class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-[560px] rounded-sm border-2 px-5 py-4 text-center text-base leading-6 {{ verification_failed|default(false) ? 'border-danger text-danger' : 'border-border text-body' }}">
        {{ verification_notice }}
      </p>
    {% endif %}

    <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-[560px] text-center text-base leading-6 text-body">
      We confirm your identity from the details you have already given us, so there is nothing more to enter here.
    </p>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-[560px] text-center text-base leading-6 text-body">
      A government-issued ID is still required by your doctor during the review, and by your pharmacy to ship your medication. <span class="font-medium text-heading">You will be asked for it there, not here.</span>
    </p>

    <form method="post" action="{{ url('/verify/') }}" novalidate>
      <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="{{ csrf_token }}" />

      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-3 rounded-sm border-2 border-dashed border-border-darker bg-background px-6 py-14 text-center opacity-60">
        <input type="file" accept="image/*,.pdf" class="sr-only" disabled aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" />
        <i data-lucide="upload" class="size-8 text-icon-muted"></i>
        <p class="text-base text-body">Sending us a copy of your ID is not part of this step.</p>
      </div>

      <button type="button" disabled aria-disabled="true" class="mt-4 inline-flex w-full cursor-not-allowed items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-sm border-2 border-border bg-background h-[41px] px-5 text-base font-medium opacity-60 sm:h-auto sm:py-4 text-heading">
        <i data-lucide="camera" class="size-5"></i>
        Take a photo of your ID
      </button>

      {% if collect_ssn|default(false) %}
        <div class="mt-6 flex items-center gap-4">
          <span class="h-px flex-1 bg-border"></span>
          <span class="text-sm font-medium text-muted">OR</span>
          <span class="h-px flex-1 bg-border"></span>
        </div>

        <label for="verify-ssn" class="sr-only">Last 4 digits of your Social Security Number</label>
        <input id="verify-ssn" name="ssn" type="text" inputmode="numeric" maxlength="4" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="Enter the last 4 digits of your SSN" class="mt-6 w-full rounded-sm border-2 border-border bg-background px-5 py-4 text-center text-base text-heading placeholder:text-muted transition-colors focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary" />
      {% endif %}

      <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="{{ url(back_path|default('/intake/medical/')) }}" class="inline-flex w-full items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-sm border-2 border-border bg-background h-[41px] px-5 text-base font-medium sm:h-auto sm:py-4 text-heading transition-colors hover:border-primary hover:text-primary focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary">
          <i data-lucide="arrow-left" class="size-[14px]"></i>
          Back
        </a>
        <button type="submit" id="verify-submit" class="inline-flex w-full items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-sm bg-primary h-[41px] px-5 text-base font-medium sm:h-auto sm:py-4 text-primary-foreground transition-colors hover:bg-primary-hover focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary-hover disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-60">
          {# The button is the only thing on this page that can move a held buyer, so it says
             so. Held means the gate has just refused them and re-running the check is the
             action the notice above points at. #}
          <span id="verify-submit-label">{{ verification_held|default(false) ? 'Try again' : 'Submit' }}</span>
          <i data-lucide="arrow-right" id="verify-submit-icon" class="size-[14px]"></i>
        </button>
      </div>
    </form>
  </section>

{% endblock %}
{% block scripts %}
{{ parent() }}
<script src="{{ asset('verify.js') }}" defer></script>
{% endblock %}
